# Docker Swarm – Short Command Notes

Assumption: Two Debian machines — one Manager and one Worker.

### 1. Initialize Swarm (Manager)

```
docker swarm init --advertise-addr MANAGER_PRIVATE_IP
```

### 2. Get Worker Join Command (Manager)

```
docker swarm join-token worker
```

### 3. Join Worker (Worker machine)

Run the join command displayed by the Manager:

```
docker swarm join --token WORKER_TOKEN MANAGER_PRIVATE_IP:2377
```

### 4. Check Nodes (Manager)

```
docker node ls
```

### 5. Create Service (Manager)

```
docker service create --name web --replicas 2 -p 8080:80 nginx
```

### 6. List Services and Tasks

```
docker service ls
docker service ps web
```

### 7. Scale Service

```
docker service scale web=4
```

### 8. Inspect Service

```
docker service inspect web
```

### 9. View Service Logs

```
docker service logs web
```

### 10. Remove Service

```
docker service rm web
```

### 11. Remove Worker from Swarm

Run on Worker:

```
docker swarm leave
```

### 12. Remove Manager from Swarm

Run on Manager:

```
docker swarm leave --force
